# Exclude the GitHub REST API response cache from version control.
# Rationale: per AAP §0.5.5 (Performance and security considerations) and
# decision-log.md Row 17 (Cache-by-Default for GitHub API), the harness caches
# every API response under data/cache/<endpoint>+<query-hash>.json so re-runs
# are reproducible without exhausting the 5,000-requests-per-hour rate limit.
# The cache directory is recreated by extract_metrics.py on each run and must
# never be committed because its contents are environment-specific (token-
# scoped, time-of-fetch dependent) and would needlessly inflate the repository.
cache/

# Exclude any per-run scratch files that extraction scripts may emit.
# Persistent extraction outputs (data/environment.json, data/inflection.json,
# data/windows.json, data/metric_<N>.json, data/consistency_report.json) are
# committed normally; only ephemeral or environment-specific files are ignored.
*.tmp
*.bak
.cache/
